<pdd-reason>Deterministic backstop for annotation-only drift: rewrites a generated annotation to the declared spelling so the surface gate converges instead of the retry loop re-emitting the same equivalent-but-different type.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-interface>
{
  "type": "module",
  "module": {
    "functions": [
      {"name": "_reconcile_declared_annotation_drift", "signature": "(existing_code: Optional[str], generated_code: str, prompt_name: str, output_path: Optional[str], language: str, prompt_content: Optional[str]) -> Optional[str]", "returns": "Optional[str]"}
    ]
  }
}
</pdd-interface>

% You are an expert Python engineer. Implement the annotation reconciler in
% `pdd/conformance/annotation_reconcile.py`.

<include>context/python_preamble.prompt</include>

% Responsibility
  Repairing the one drift class a retry loop cannot converge on its own: a
  generated signature that differs from its declaration ONLY in how a type is
  spelled. Asking a model to re-emit `object` when it keeps producing `Any`
  fails indefinitely; rewriting the annotation is deterministic (#1968).

% Non-responsibilities
  Decides nothing about whether a generation passes - it runs before the gate and
  hands back source for the gate to judge. Never repairs structural drift.

% Vocabulary
  - **annotation-only drift**: matching parameter names, order, kinds and
    defaults, differing solely in annotation text.
  - **reconcile**: rewrite the generated source so the offending annotations read
    as declared.

% Contract rules
  R1. It MUST return replacement source only when at least one annotation was
      reconciled, and nothing otherwise. It MUST NEVER alter a generation that
      would otherwise pass.
  R2. It MUST run before the public-surface gate. When it returns source, that
      source is what the gate judges and what the writer persists.
  R3. Only symbols declared in a `type: "module"` interface are eligible.
  R4. A symbol is eligible ONLY when its sole difference from the declaration is
      annotation spelling. Any structural difference - a parameter added,
      removed, reordered, re-kinded, or re-defaulted - MUST disqualify that
      symbol and leave it to the gate and the repair loop.
  R5. Only annotations the gate would reject MUST be rewritten. A merely
      interchangeable spelling, such as `Dict` against `dict`, MUST be left
      alone - churning it would produce a diff with no behavioral meaning.
  R6. Rewrites MUST preserve the rest of the file byte-for-byte; only the
      offending annotation regions change.
  R7. It MUST be fail-safe: if the reconciled source no longer parses, the entire
      rewrite MUST be discarded and nothing returned. A broken file is worse than
      an unconverged one.
  R8. `PDD_SKIP_ANNOTATION_RECONCILE` MUST bypass it entirely.
  R9. Text handling MUST be correct for non-ASCII source. Offsets computed in
      one unit and applied in another corrupt files containing non-ASCII
      characters.

% Inputs and outputs
  Given the previous code, the generated code, and the prompt, it returns either
  the reconciled source or nothing. It never raises for ordinary drift.

% Dependencies
  Standard library `ast`; the declared-interface reader from
  `.declared_surface`; and the annotation comparator from
  `pdd.interface_semantics`.
